---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseStudyHeader from '../../components/CaseStudyHeader.astro';
import EvidencePanel from '../../components/EvidencePanel.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const facts = [
  { num: '1.74%', lbl: 'Observed uplift against the preregistered advancement gate' },
  { num: '5%', lbl: 'Preregistered advancement gate — not met' },
  { num: 'SHA-256', lbl: 'Protocol and input freeze for reproducibility' },
  { num: '0', lbl: 'Strategies advanced — the honest outcome' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Designing research to reject weak conclusions — Fabio Valente"
  description="Case study: a preregistered, independently reviewed validation workflow for a trading experiment that ended in an auditable no-advance decision."
>
  <CaseStudyHeader
    num="03"
    title="Designing research to reject weak conclusions"
    status="VALIDATION & QA / AUDITED, INCONCLUSIVE"
    lead="A trustworthy research pipeline needs to reject attractive results when the evidence is not strong enough. I specified validation gates and independent review for a data-driven trading experiment, and the final decision was not to advance it."
  >
    <div class="facts-row">
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="num" style="font-size:24px;">{f.num}</div>
          <div class="lbl">{f.lbl}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </CaseStudyHeader>

  <div class="container case-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Exploratory strategies can appear promising because of look-ahead, cherry-picking, data
        leakage, parameter selection, or inconsistent reruns. Here, the requirement was an
        auditable process with a credible decision, not a favorable backtest.
      </p>

      <h2>My role</h2>
      <p>
        I specified research requirements and acceptance criteria, requested protocol freezing and
        independent audit, reviewed findings, and approved the no-advance decision. AI agents built
        and operated the supporting analysis engines; this is a case about experimental governance
        and testing, not independently authored quantitative software or realized trading profits.
      </p>

      <h2>Process and guardrails</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Define the hypothesis and preregister advancement criteria.</li>
        <li>Freeze protocol and inputs with SHA-256 hashes to aid reproducibility.</li>
        <li>Apply chronological development, validation, and evaluation splits.</li>
        <li>Execute experiments with recorded settings and results.</li>
        <li>Use separate reviewers for reproducibility, look-ahead, and potential artifacts.</li>
        <li>Compare results to the stated criteria; reject or hold without moving goalposts.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>A process that can say no</h2>

      <div class="diagram-panel">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 680 190" role="img" aria-label="Validation timeline: develop, validate, evaluate with chronological splits, independent audit, and a no-advance decision. A textual comparison shows observed uplift of 1.74 percent versus a 5 percent gate.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="arr3" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#3E5C76"></path>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <style>
            .n3 { fill:#FFFFFF; stroke:#C9CFD6; }
            .r3 { fill:#F7F1E6; stroke:#8A6D3B; }
            .t3 { fill:#23282E; font:600 13px Manrope,sans-serif; }
            .s3 { fill:#7A7F86; font:500 9.5px 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.06em; }
            .a3 { stroke:#3E5C76; stroke-width:1.5; fill:none; }
            .gate3 { fill:#8A6D3B; font:700 15px 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; }
          </style>
          <rect class="n3" x="10" y="30" width="100" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t3" x="60" y="53" text-anchor="middle">Develop</text>
          <text class="s3" x="60" y="70" text-anchor="middle">EARLY SPLIT</text>
          <path class="a3" d="M110,58 L128,58" marker-end="url(#arr3)"></path>

          <rect class="n3" x="130" y="30" width="100" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t3" x="180" y="53" text-anchor="middle">Validate</text>
          <text class="s3" x="180" y="70" text-anchor="middle">LATER SPLIT</text>
          <path class="a3" d="M230,58 L248,58" marker-end="url(#arr3)"></path>

          <rect class="n3" x="250" y="30" width="100" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t3" x="300" y="53" text-anchor="middle">Evaluate</text>
          <text class="s3" x="300" y="70" text-anchor="middle">HELD-OUT</text>
          <path class="a3" d="M350,58 L368,58" marker-end="url(#arr3)"></path>

          <rect class="n3" x="370" y="30" width="130" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t3" x="435" y="53" text-anchor="middle">Independent audit</text>
          <text class="s3" x="435" y="70" text-anchor="middle">SEPARATE REVIEWERS</text>
          <path class="a3" d="M500,58 L518,58" marker-end="url(#arr3)"></path>

          <rect class="r3" x="520" y="24" width="150" height="68" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t3" x="595" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8A6D3B">DECISION</text>
          <text class="s3" x="595" y="70" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8A6D3B">INCONCLUSIVE / NO ADVANCE</text>

          <line x1="60" y1="130" x2="620" y2="130" stroke="#E3DED4" stroke-width="1"></line>
          <text class="s3" x="60" y="152">OBSERVED UPLIFT</text>
          <text class="gate3" x="60" y="176">1.74%</text>
          <line x1="480" y1="136" x2="480" y2="182" stroke="#8A6D3B" stroke-width="2"></line>
          <text class="s3" x="500" y="152">PREREGISTERED GATE</text>
          <text class="gate3" x="500" y="176">5%</text>
          <text class="s3" x="300" y="186" text-anchor="middle">GATE NOT MET → DO NOT ADVANCE (TEXTUAL LABELS — NOT A PERFORMANCE CHART)</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="caption">CONCEPTUAL, SANITIZED WORKFLOW</p>
      </div>
      <p class="scroll-hint">← Scroll the diagram sideways for readable text →</p>

      <h2>Observed result</h2>
      <p>
        The reviewed experiment reported <strong>1.74% uplift against a preregistered 5%
        advancement gate</strong>, so the decision was <strong>INCONCLUSIVE / NO ADVANCE</strong>.
        Independent review accepted that adverse conclusion with limitations. The useful output was
        a documented, defensible decision—not evidence of profitable live trading.
      </p>

      <h2>Related research practice</h2>
      <p>
        In related trading research, I coordinate backtesting, walk-forward analysis, Monte Carlo
        assessment, and risk/robustness reviews. These are research methods and validation
        workflows—not claims of independently profitable strategies.
      </p>

      <div class="limits">
        <h3>Limitations</h3>
        <p>
          This work is not a verified investable strategy, a live-trading product, or proof of
          profitable returns. Proprietary strategy rules, licensed data, account details, and any
          chart implying a verified track record are deliberately omitted.
        </p>
      </div>

      <EvidencePanel />
    </div>

    <nav class="case-nav" aria-label="Case study navigation">
      <a href="/work/research-automation/">← Previous: Turning recurring research into a verifiable workflow</a>
      <a href="/work/engineering-operations/">Next: Coordinating high-stakes operational work →</a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <ContactCTA />
</BaseLayout>
